+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends an API key as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in
+the data (`apiKeys`, see `docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key, or a key that is not known, is `401 unauthorized`; a known key whose
+role does not allow the route is `403 forbidden`. Every request other than
+`GET` made with a known key (whatever its status) writes an audit entry;
+`GET /audit` lists them newest first:
+
+    [{ "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "dev cook", "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }]
+
